INT. SELF-STORAGE UNIT 114 - DAY

ON CAMERA: a roll-up door half open, daylight on concrete. The camera operator's breathing is audible.

Hollis, 60s, in a sweat-stained Stetson, kneels over a trunk. Behind him, boxes stacked to the ceiling, saddles, a dented tin lantern.

A woman stands in the doorway with her arms crossed. She does not give her name. She has a leather satchel and a very flat voice.

HOLLIS
Told the office it was all family stuff. Photographs. My granddad's saddle.

THE WOMAN
And the brand book.

HOLLIS
Didn't say a word about no brand book.

THE WOMAN
You didn't have to.

Hollis opens the trunk. Nothing. Dust.

HOLLIS
Well, it ain't here.

Hollis's phone RINGS. He answers on speaker.

WADE (V.O.)
(tinny)
Pa? You in there yet? Don't open nothing till I get there.

HOLLIS
Too late, son.

WADE (V.O.)
Is somebody with you?

Hollis looks at the woman. She looks at the camera. For a long time none of them say anything.

THE WOMAN
Tell him it's Odalys. Tell him I came the long way round.

HOLLIS
(into the phone)
It's Odalys.

WADE (V.O.)
(a pause, then flat)
I'm ten minutes out. Stay put.

The line goes dead. Hollis puts the phone in his pocket and does not look up.

HOLLIS
He ain't gonna be happy.

ODALYS
No.

HOLLIS
You gonna wait?

ODALYS
I have waited thirty years, Mr. Hollis. Ten minutes is nothing.

CAL
(behind the camera)
Are we still rolling?

Nobody answers him.
